Security Resource Prevention:- It all about detecting issues, finding bugs, vulnerabilities, and things of that nature within your aws environment. 

Aws Inspector:- It will actually scan the workloads running on aws for vulnerabilities and undesired network exposures. 
		When vulnerabilities are found, inspector produces a report with the findings.
		Re-runs scans whenever changes that could introduce new vulnerabilities are made.

Aws GuardDuty:- It is the service that identifies threats by continuously monitoring the activity on your aws infra.
		It detect usual pattern and behaviour of you aws account. if it detect anything abnormal, it will notify you. 
		
Amazon detective:- It actually grab logs and findings from couple of different services. Like guardDuty, CloudTrail, VPC flow logs. it takes all of those. with use of machine learning to actually create advanced visualisation and interactive dashbord.
To easier to troubleshoot and root cause any issue. 
 
Aws Config:- Aws config tracks and audits the configuration of aws resources over time.
	     Anything change in the resources it track all in aws configs. 

Aws Security Hub:- It takes finding from Amazon Inspector and Aws GuradDuty and few other locations. it going to centralised all of the security alerts so that you can see it all in a single pane of glass. It has automate security check as well. 

Cloud Trail:- It tracks user activity within aws account. So anytime user perform any action whithin aws, an event is going to logged in cloud trail. It logs all the unauthorised activity done by the user. 

Security Lake:- It collects security logs and events from multiple different sources. It aggregrate all of those logs in one central location. It convert that logs into a storage and query efficient parquet format as well as transfer data to the open cybersecutiry schema framework open source schema. veriety of diff subscriber consume that data from security lake so they can then process. 

Aws Macie:- It autometically discover sensative data. It will generate an inventry report of your s3 bucket can scan for objects that may contain sensative data. it will notify you so that you can take necessary action.
