Security Resource management:- All of these required configuration and specific rule and policies that we have to define.

Firewall Manager:- It is a security management service that allow you to centrally configure and managed firewall rules of all of your accounts, applications and aws organisations. It is a central place to manage all of your rules. 

Resource Access Manager:- It help you securaly share resuorces across accounts, organisation and organisational unit. SO you could create a resource once like privet subnet in aws account one then have it shared among all the other acoounts. So account one and account two can actually deploy EC2 instances into that subnet thats define in account one. It just make it really easy to share resources amongest multiple accounts. 

Aws Cognito:- It helps implement customer indentity and access management for mobile and web application. It help you implement login and sign-up functionality to any application very easily and you get social authentication as well. It manage all of the user credentials. You dont have to manage and store all the information. 

Aws Identity Center:- It allows you to manage sign-in security for all of your users in a central place and you can grant these users access to multiple aws accounts and resources across multiple aws accounts. You get a single place where you get to manage all of the users and then give them access to all of you diff accounts. 

Secrets Manager:- Credential can be stored and managed in Aws Secrets Manager. The application can dynamically pull the secrets from the secret manager. So we have to hard quote it into your application code. If has autometic rotaion feature for your secrets. 

Aws Certificate Manager:- It handles the complexity of creating, storing, and renewing pubilc and private certificates that can be used to protect aws websites and services. You can send encrypted data to Elastic Load balancer, CloudFront, Api Gateway and varity of different services. So you dont have to managed those certificates yourself. 

Aws Private Certificate Authority:- It manages and aws private certificate authority for you so that you can generate privet certificate within you organisation. Whether its for on-prem or in cloud resources you can generate privet cert for them so you can send encrypted traffic.  This service does not generate publicaly trusted certificate. It is for the internal resources. 

Key Management service (KMS):- It allows you create and manage all of you cryptographic keys. For sensatice data you never want to store it in plain text. Instead you want to encrypt it. And so you'll make use of a cryptographic key that will encrypt the data. So the data is encrypted, nobady else will be able to read it. if you want to decrypt the data make use same key to decrypt the data to get original plain text object. so for the keys handaling and decryption process, you can managed them yourself, or you can make use of a serice like Aws KMS. you can also enable autometic key encryption. It is a tool for managing the cryptographic keys. 

Cloud Hardward Security module (HSM):- It is the place where you store all of your cryptographic keys. Anytime you need to perform a cryptographic operation like encryption or decryption. sent a request to hsm and thats going to perform the decryption process. Sice all of the keys are stored in once single device, it little bit more secure and easier to manage because you know whare they are your keys are scattered in multiple servers. 







